the court in france has found former  president nicolas sarkozy guilty of  corruption and  influence peddling the judge has handed  sarkozy a three-year prison sentence  two of which are suspended the 66 year  old  is the second leader in france's modern  history to be convicted  of corruption natasha butler is live for  us at the court in paris natasha  run us through uh what exactly he's been  found guilty of  and does this mean that we're going to  see a former president now heading to  prison  yes uh nicholas sarkozy becoming  the first former french president to be  handed  a jail sentence he was found guilty by  the court here  in paris of corruption and influence  peddling and he's been handed  a three-year jail sentence so we  understand two years  suspended the third year he may be able  to carry out  under house arrest now lawyers for  nicolas sarkozy say  that he does intend to appeal now this  case uh  focused on an incident in 2014 in which  sarkozy  was charged with trying to influence the  magistrate trying to offer this  magistrate  a top job in return for information  into another investigation which was  being carried out at the time by police  on nicolas sarkozy over uh campaign  funds  now nicholas sarkozy during the trial  always protested his innocence he said  that  uh that he had been the victim of a  political smear campaign but it seems  that the judge here in paris disagreed  handing out this uh jail sentence a  devastating blow indeed  uh to nicolas sarkozy so what then might  this mean natasha  for sarkozy's political ambitions  [Music]  well sarkozy served as president of  france a conservative president from  2007 to  but since he left office since he left  uh the elysee he has really been you  might say  trying to stage a political comeback in  2017  he even ran once again uh for the  presidency  and uh over the years he certainly tried  to position himself as a hope for the  conservative party perhaps for another  presidential election campaign but you'd  have to say that this guilty verdict  cerny  will deal a blow to those ambitions it  would be hard to imagine  that a former president with now a jail  sentence to contend with could possibly  uh take the center stage once again  uh politically so very disappointing for  sarkozy  uh his reputation in tatters you might  say but as i said the former french  leader  making it very clear that he will appeal  okay thank you for that  natasha butler live for us at the court  in paris
 

